cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This is a public-domain legislative research draft, released under CC0 1.0.
  Please cite the publication version and commit so readers can identify the
  text reviewed.
title: "Frontier Artificial Intelligence Officer Certification Act (New York RAISE Act research draft)"
abstract: >-
  A research draft adding a new section 1422-a to article 44-B of the New York
  General Business Law, amending the Responsible AI Safety and Education
  (RAISE) Act to require named natural persons at large frontier developers to
  sign for the developer's compliance. The enacted RAISE Act, chapter 96 of the
  laws of 2026, places transparency, catastrophic-risk assessment, frontier AI
  framework and incident-reporting duties on the developer as an entity, and
  bars materially false or misleading statements about catastrophic risk. Its
  enacted text contains no independent audit requirement, no signature
  requirement, no certification requirement, and no duty owed by any natural
  person. The draft adds a deployment certification or truthful acknowledgment
  of material noncompliance, an annual certification, personal and
  non-delegable duties of reasonable inquiry and response, a searchable public
  register of required signers, civil enforcement against a signer for breach
  of that signer's own duty, and personal payment of individual penalties
  without corporate indemnification, insurance, reimbursement or compensation
  offset. It uses the RAISE Act's existing definitions, regulator and coverage
  thresholds rather than creating a separate regulatory system, and creates no
  new criminal offense and no private right of action. Public-domain research
  draft; never introduced or enacted; no completed review claimed.
